{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the word is rare (יקירה)</b> — like ויקר פדיון נפשם, which has no [satisfying] interpretation." "<b>Elohin</b> — these are the exalted angels, who are true forms and are not like bodies, and the souls are derived from them, like light that emanates from the sun. And the souls are bodies; therefore they do not know hidden things except a little, and in night visions, when the souls are not occupied with the needs of the body. And one who knows the secret of the soul will testify to my words."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra says שלא מצאה טעם, literally 'it found no reason'; rendered as 'has no interpretation.'", 1 "The clause והנשמות הם גופות is textually difficult given the preceding contrast; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:10.520286088Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}